# Spring Boot configuration

Put infrastructure endpoints in `application.yml`. Use environment variables with local defaults. Never hardcode credentials.

```yaml
# ✅ GOOD
spring:
  datasource:
    url: ${DATABASE_URL:jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/appdb}
    username: ${DATABASE_USERNAME:app}
    password: ${DATABASE_PASSWORD:changeme}
  data:
    redis:
      host: ${REDIS_HOST:localhost}
      port: ${REDIS_PORT:6379}
```

- Default Redis host: `${REDIS_HOST:localhost}`
- Talk to Postgres and Redis by Kubernetes Service names in cluster, not pod IPs.
